  "published": "2026-11-26",
  "updated": "2026-11-26",
  "intro": "Brex, Mercury, Relay, Expensify and BILL are the five business money tools covered as Ramp alternatives. Published entry prices are $0 at Ramp Free, Brex Essentials, Mercury, Relay Starter and Expensify Submit, while paid plans run from $5 per member per month on Expensify Collect to $12 per user per month on Brex Premium and $15 per user per month on Ramp Plus.\n\n[Ramp](https://www.ramp.com/pricing) sells a Free plan at $0 per user per month with corporate cards, unlimited cards, travel and expense management, and accounts payable bill payment by Automated Clearing House (ACH), card, check and wire. Ramp Plus lists at $15 per user per month plus an unpublished team-size platform fee (with a 20% discount on annual billing), adding multi-entity support, artificial intelligence (AI) expense reviews, custom user roles and integrations for NetSuite and Sage Intacct. Ramp also lists a footnoted 4.61% yield in a Ramp Investment Account with no fees, minimum deposits or transfer caps, alongside 2% on cash in a Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) insured checking account.\n\nAt The Modern Wallet, we lay out published fee schedules so business owners can calculate their operational costs before selecting financial software. For related banking and card shortlists, read our [best business bank accounts roundup](/roundup/best-business-bank-accounts/), our [best business credit cards roundup](/roundup/best-business-credit-cards/) and our [best accounting software for freelancers](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) guide. You can also review our [Brex alternatives](/alternatives/brex/) guide, our [Mercury alternatives](/alternatives/mercury/) comparison and our [comparison hub](/compare/).",
